      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg** three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day** total, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you verified the dose."
